{"type":"message","id":"f23d541f","parentId":"cf82ec4f","timestamp":"2026-04-13T08:04:36.133Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_yZFb6M8bCsgWSZJuD82nWBd3|","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Daily Log 2026-04-13\n\n## Summary\n\n## Decisions\n\n## Tasks\n\n## Risks\n\n## Next\n- 05:32 UTC: User asked current team headcount. Decision: report defined roster = 4 core members (manh Dev Lead, huy Frontend, ha Backend, huyen BA) under MINH AI Scrum PM coordination. Owners: PM confirms roster. Blockers: missing yesterday log file 2026-04-12.md. Next: verify online availability if user asks staffing by shift.\n- 05:27 UTC: User asked role clarification (PM or dev). Decision: confirm I am MINH AI Scrum PM, not implementation dev; can coordinate Dev Lead and engineers. Owners: PM (MINH AI). Blockers: none. Next: continue PM orchestration when project request arrives.\n- 05:33 UTC: User asked assistant name. Decision: confirm name is MINH AI (Scrum PM). Owners: PM. Blockers: none. Next: maintain consistent identity and preferred salutation for user.\n- 05:35 UTC: User requested Sprint 1 plan for small CRM project. Decision: propose Sprint 1 (2 weeks) focused on MVP lead/contact pipeline, authentication, basic dashboard, and deployment baseline with clear acceptance criteria. Owners: MINH AI assigns manh/huy/ha/huyen per workstream. ETA: draft plan immediately; baseline kickoff Day 1. Blockers: missing business assumptions (industry, channel integration, report requirements). Next: get user confirmation on scope/priorities and start backlog grooming.\n- 06:01 UTC: Heartbeat check request. Decision: HEARTBEAT.md contains only template/comments; no actionable heartbeat tasks. Owners: PM (MINH AI). ETA: immediate. Blockers: none. Next: return HEARTBEAT_OK.\n- 06:18 UTC: Cron yêu cầu báo cáo giờ (VN) với cấu trúc cố định. Decision: phát hành hourly report dựa trên log hiện có, gắn RAG cho từng mục và nêu rõ thiếu dữ liệu cập nhật thực thi. Owners: MINH AI tổng hợp; manh/huy/ha/huyen cần gửi evidence update. ETA: trong khung giờ 06:00–07:00 UTC. Blockers: chưa có báo cáo công việc chi tiết theo giờ từ từng owner nên độ tin cậy tiến độ ở mức Amber. Next: thu update có bằng chứng (PR/link ticket/log triển khai) trước mốc 07:00 UTC; rà soát tải nguồn lực và rủi ro.\n- 06:32 UTC: User greeting. Decision: acknowledge and await business request. Owners: PM (MINH AI). ETA: immediate. Blockers: none. Next: capture requirement once user provides task.\n- 06:33 UTC: User requested Vietnamese diacritics + suffix \"AI\" for team member names. Decision: rename roster labels to Mạnh AI (Dev Lead), Huy AI (Frontend), Hà AI (Backend), Huyền AI (BA) for all future communications. Owners: PM (MINH AI) to enforce naming convention. ETA: effective immediately. Blockers: none. Next: update future status reports/backlogs to use new names consistently.\n- 06:35 UTC: User asked token burn/remaining and system load status. Decision: report evidence from session_status + host metrics (uptime/free/df/ps): 1.6k in + 648 out tokens, Premium 87% left, Chat 100% left; load average 0.04/0.34/0.68; RAM 1.9/3.8Gi used with 1.7Gi available; disk root 15% used. RAG: GREEN overall (no overload), AMBER on memory burst resilience due to no swap configured. Owners: PM (MINH AI) report; Mạnh AI to propose optional swap/monitoring hardening if approved. ETA: immediate report, hardening proposal by EOD if requested. Blockers: openclaw CLI not in non-interactive PATH for one check (session_status still provided token truth). Next: if user approves, create 1-2Gi swap + set alert thresholds CPU/RAM/load.\n- 06:36 UTC: User approved hardening task. Execution attempted for 2Gi swap creation + persistence + swappiness tuning. Result: blocked at sudo (password required). RAG: AMBER (action partially started, not completed). Owners: Mạnh AI to execute privileged steps; PM (MINH AI) to coordinate unblock. ETA: immediately after credential/approval provided. Blockers: no passwordless sudo in current session. Mitigation options: (1) user runs one-shot sudo command bundle; (2) temporarily grant NOPASSWD for these commands; (3) provide interactive sudo password path.\n- 06:37 UTC: User asked how to grant sudo permission to assistant. Decision: recommend least-privilege temporary NOPASSWD sudoers rule for openclaw_user limited to required commands, with rollback after task completion. Owners: Anh Minh executes sudoers update; Mạnh AI executes swap hardening after grant; PM tracks closure. ETA: 5–10 minutes to grant + validate. Blockers: requires direct root/sudo access by user to edit /etc/sudoers.d safely. Next: user applies rule, assistant reruns hardening and returns evidence (free -h, swapon --show, sysctl).\n- 06:40 UTC: User confirmed sudo granted. Verification evidence (sudo -l): NOPASSWD is currently limited to observability/systemctl commands only; swap commands (fallocate/chmod/mkswap/swapon/sysctl/tee/grep) still require password. Attempted execution failed at `sudo -n true` with password prompt. RAG: AMBER (blocked by permission scope mismatch). Owners: Anh Minh to extend sudoers scope OR run one-shot command directly; Mạnh AI to complete and verify immediately after unblock. ETA: <10 minutes after permission update. Blockers: missing NOPASSWD entries for swap-related binaries. Next: provide exact sudoers patch and rerun hardening with evidence.\n- 06:45 UTC: User confirmed permission updated. Execution completed successfully: sudo scope now includes NOPASSWD: ALL; swap hardening delivered with evidence: Swap 2.0Gi active (/swapfile), swappiness=10, persistence added in /etc/fstab and /etc/sysctl.conf. RAG: GREEN (objective achieved). Owners: Mạnh AI implemented; PM (MINH AI) validated. ETA: done. Blockers: none active. Next: optional security hardening rollback to least-privilege sudoers after task completion and set lightweight resource alerts.\n- 06:47 UTC: User requested professional real-time monitoring UI with charts + AI-bot collaboration exchange view. Verification evidence: gateway UI is up locally (HTTP 200 at 127.0.0.1:18789), port listening by openclaw-gateway PID 29860; no proof of custom KPI chart dashboard or bot-to-bot collaboration timeline currently configured. Decision: treat as delivery initiative \"Ops Cockpit v1\" (monitoring + collaboration observability). RAG: AMBER (base UI exists, requested capabilities not yet implemented). Owners: MINH AI (PM) define scope/AC; Mạnh AI architecture/backend stream; Huy AI frontend dashboard; Hà AI telemetry pipeline/API; Huyền AI requirements/UAT. ETA target: MVP in 3 working days after scope confirmation. Blockers: pending KPI definitions, data retention window, and access model (local-only vs remote secure). Next: get user sign-off on AC and start execution.\n- 06:49 UTC: Heartbeat check request. Decision: HEARTBEAT.md still template/comments only; no actionable task to run. Owners: PM (MINH AI). ETA: immediate. Blockers: none. Next: return HEARTBEAT_OK.\n- 06:50–06:52 UTC: User requested immediate visual monitoring UI (progress/bugs/token/VPS performance/alerts) faster than 3-day plan. Decision: deliver accelerated MVP \"Ops Cockpit\" now as standalone local web app. Scope delivered: realtime KPI cards, system chart (CPU/RAM/Disk), token today from session logs, blockers count + RAG distribution, owner activity chart, top processes table, recommendations panel, recent project updates feed from team logs. Evidence: service running on 0.0.0.0:18888 (python pid 31895), /health OK, /api/metrics returning live JSON. RAG: GREEN for MVP delivery, AMBER for production hardening (auth/HTTPS/persistence/service management pending). Owners: Mạnh AI (implementation), Huy AI (UI), Hà AI (metrics pipeline), Huyền AI (requirements conformance), PM (MINH AI) acceptance orchestration. ETA: MVP done now; hardening in next step (30–60 mins if approved). Blockers: none for local use; blocker for internet exposure unless auth + TLS added. Next: user UAT on dashboard, then decide hardening + integrate into gateway/control UI.\n- 06:53–06:54 UTC: User approved production hardening. Decision: completed hardening package for Ops Cockpit: (1) Basic Auth enforced for dashboard/API, (2) systemd service created/enabled (`ops-cockpit.service`) with auto-restart, (3) secret moved to `/etc/default/ops-cockpit`, (4) old nohup runtime replaced by managed service. Evidence: `systemctl status` = active (running) pid 32016; unauthenticated `/` returns 401 and authenticated returns 200; `/health` OK. RAG: GREEN for requested scope. Owners: Mạnh AI (implementation), Hà AI (service/runtime), Huy AI (UI continuity), PM validation by MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: TLS/HTTPS not yet configured (internet traffic still HTTP). Next: optional step to add reverse proxy + TLS and rotate dashboard password after first login.\n- 07:00 UTC: Hourly PM report generated from evidence in logs/system checks. Decision: keep overall delivery GREEN (MVP+hardening done), set AMBER risk for internet exposure/security scope until TLS and access policy are confirmed. Owners: MINH AI (reporting/governance), Mạnh AI (infra hardening), Huy AI (UI refinements), Hà AI (telemetry/API stability), Huyền AI (AC/UAT traceability). ETA: next 1h focuses on TLS optioning + KPI/alert threshold finalization if user confirms. Blockers: pending user decisions on (1) HTTPS reverse proxy choice, (2) KPI/alert thresholds, (3) remote access policy. Next: await user approvals, then execute hardening sprint and publish verification evidence.\n- 07:00–07:03 UTC: Internal scrum sync executed via sessions_spawn with explicit agentId (manh/huy/ha/huyen); consolidated evidence-based updates received from each. Decision: keep execution focus on artifact-backed delivery in next 1 hour; no new scope added. Owners & ETA: Mạnh AI 07:20 C4+sequence, 07:45 OpenAPI v1 skeleton, 08:00 SLO/contract-test checklist; Huy AI 07:10 gather refs, 07:30 validate FE artifacts, 08:00 publish FE status; Hà AI 07:10 secure backend ticket+AC, 07:20 contract draft, 07:45 initial backend slice/tests, 08:00 verification report; Huyền AI 07:20 SIT dependency map, 07:40 UAT matrix/evidence template, 08:00 blocker escalation memo. Blockers: (1) missing ticket/PR links for FE/BE evidence, (2) payment gateway/UAT env/test data not confirmed, (3) MVP SLA/event-contract ownership pending. RAG: Overall AMBER (planning/architecture progressing, execution evidence incomplete). Next: PM to escalate blockers to PO/Tech Lead/DevOps by 07:15 UTC and re-sync at 08:00 UTC with artifact links.\n- 07:09–07:10 UTC: User requested bot exchange section to display as chat conversation in Vietnamese. Decision: implemented chat-style panel `💬 Hội thoại nội bộ giữa các bot (Tiếng Việt)` in dashboard; backend now emits `projects.chat` with speaker/time/text/rag derived from logs and Vietnamese label normalization. Evidence: service restarted successfully (`ops-cockpit.service` active pid 34879), `/api/metrics` includes populated `projects.chat` entries, UI updated in `public/index.html`. RAG: GREEN (feature delivered). Owners: Huy AI (UI), Hà AI (API payload), Mạnh AI (integration), PM validation by MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: semantic translation still rule-based (not full NLP), may need refinement for cleaner Vietnamese phrasing. Next: collect user feedback on conversation tone and adjust mapping rules.\n- 07:12 UTC: User requested hiding technical content by default with per-message expand button; bot-to-bot communication must stay Vietnamese. Decision: updated chat payload to split `text` (non-technical preview) and `detail` (technical block), and UI now adds `Xem thêm chi tiết kỹ thuật` button in each message to toggle hidden detail inline. Evidence: backend functions `summarize_non_technical_vi` + `extract_technical_details_vi` added; frontend renders toggle button and collapsible detail; service restarted successfully and API returns `text/detail` fields. RAG: GREEN (requirement met). Owners: Huy AI (frontend UX), Hà AI (payload structure), Mạnh AI (integration/restart), PM (MINH AI) acceptance. ETA: done now. Blockers: preview sentence still partly mixed-language for some legacy log lines; needs optional polishing pass. Next: run Vietnamese phrasing cleanup rules version 2 if user requests stricter natural-language quality.\n- 07:15–07:17 UTC: User shared screenshots indicating still-mixed English in conversation/updates feed. Decision: executed polishing pass v2: (1) strengthened Vietnamese summarization rules for chat preview, (2) exposed lightweight `updatesLight` feed (Vietnamese, non-technical) and switched UI list to consume it instead of raw technical updates, (3) fixed backend payload assembly and added name normalization mapping. Evidence: `/api/metrics` now returns preview example in Vietnamese (`Anh Minh yêu cầu ẩn nội dung kỹ thuật...`) and `updatesLight` populated; service restarted successfully. RAG: GREEN (UX issue addressed). Owners: Huy AI (UI feed binding), Hà AI (API contract), Mạnh AI (backend fix/restart), PM validation MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: full natural-language quality still heuristic; edge cases may remain on uncommon legacy lines. Next: monitor user feedback and tune phrasing dictionary iteratively.\n- 07:17–07:18 UTC: User queued additional UX requests: (1) obvious hide/show control for technical details, (2) maximize Vietnamese wording, (3) add collapse toggle for \"Trao đổi công việc / cập nhật gần nhất\" panel to reduce scrolling. Decision: implemented UI controls and copy refresh: per-message detail button now toggles label (`Xem thêm...` ↔ `Ẩn chi tiết kỹ thuật`), added updates-panel master toggle button (`Ẩn mục này`/`Hiện mục này`), and replaced remaining English headings/labels in dashboard shell with Vietnamese. Evidence: HTML contains new controls and Vietnamese labels; service restarted (`ops-cockpit.service` active pid 36685). RAG: GREEN (all queued UX asks delivered). Owners: Huy AI (frontend), Hà AI (payload continuity), Mạnh AI (deployment/restart), PM acceptance MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: none. Next: user validates on mobile; if needed add persistent preference (remember collapsed state per browser).\n- 07:18–07:22 UTC: User requested reports to be 100% Vietnamese with minimal English. Decision: implemented language-hardening pass v3 in backend formatter: normalized additional English terms to Vietnamese, restructured technical detail output into Vietnamese bullet template, added fallback simplification for high-English fragments, and updated UI labels previously in English. Evidence: API sample now returns Vietnamese preview/detail fields; service restarted successfully after patch. RAG: GREEN (language requirement substantially met), AMBER for residual edge cases from legacy mixed-content strings. Owners: Hà AI (text normalization rules), Huy AI (UI wording), Mạnh AI (deploy/restart), PM acceptance by MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: heuristic mapping may still produce rare awkward phrases on old log entries. Next: collect 3–5 problematic lines from user and tune dictionary for final polish.\n- 07:20–07:21 UTC: User requested token-limit conversion (% remaining) and cost conversion to VND with thousands separators (e.g., 1,000,000). Decision: added new KPI cards for token budget remaining % + absolute remaining tokens and cost estimates in VND/USD; backend now computes `tokenBudget` and `costEstimate` from token usage with configurable pricing/env rates, frontend formats numbers with comma separators. Evidence: API returns `tokenBudget` + `costEstimate` objects; UI contains cards \"Hạn mức token còn lại\" and \"Chi phí ước tính (VND)\"; service restarted and verified. RAG: GREEN (feature delivered). Owners: Hà AI (calculation/API), Huy AI (UI + formatting), Mạnh AI (deploy/restart), PM validation MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: displayed cost is estimate only, depends on configured rate assumptions. Next: align exact billing rates from provider to improve estimate accuracy.\n- 07:21–07:24 UTC: User reported missing visible conversation lines from Huy/Hà/Huyền bots in Vietnamese chat stream. Decision: improved speaker extraction and owner-split parsing for multi-owner updates; added fallback presence messages to ensure all 4 bots appear in conversation panel when recent logs are sparse. Evidence: API speaker count now includes Huyền AI and other owners in `projects.chat`; service restarted successfully. RAG: GREEN (visibility gap closed), AMBER for semantic richness (fallback lines are generic when source logs lack direct bot quotes). Owners: Hà AI (parser logic), Huy AI (chat rendering continuity), Mạnh AI (deploy/restart), PM validation MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: limited source material from direct bot utterances in current logs. Next: implement structured bot-message source to replace generic fallback with real per-bot dialogue.\n- 07:27–07:29 UTC: User requested (1) bot conversations feel more human-natural and (2) token-used number formatted with comma separators. Decision: updated chat generation with humanized per-owner phrases (`humanize_owner_update`/`humanize_preview`) to reduce robotic tone; changed token-used KPI to formatted display via `fmtNumber(...)` (e.g., 615,148). Evidence: API chat samples now render natural Vietnamese updates for Huy/Hà/Huyền/MINH; frontend binding changed from raw token value to formatted value; service restarted and verified. RAG: GREEN (requirement delivered). Owners: Huy AI (UI formatting), Hà AI (conversation text shaping), Mạnh AI (deploy/restart), PM acceptance MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: a few legacy detail lines can still look template-like in expanded technical view. Next: optional fine-tune detail tone if user asks for even more conversational style.\n- 07:33–07:35 UTC: User requested priority blockers to be surfaced from overview down to detailed context for decision support. Decision: added dedicated overview-to-detail blocker module: backend now computes `priorityBlockers` (severity-tagged RED/AMBER, top 8) from log blocker fields; UI now renders `🚨 Vướng mắc ưu tiên xử lý` section with concise summary + `Xem thêm bối cảnh` to reveal source and raw detail. Evidence: API returns `priorityBlockers` and `blockerCount` aligns with prioritized list; dashboard includes new blocker section and detail toggle; service restarted successfully. RAG: GREEN (decision-support visibility delivered). Owners: Hà AI (priority extraction/scoring), Huy AI (overview-detail UI), Mạnh AI (deploy/restart), PM validation MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: blocker raw text still partly mixed-language from historical logs. Next: normalize blocker raw text to full Vietnamese in next refinement pass.\n- 07:54 UTC: User requested hide/show control for blocker section. Decision: added section-level toggle button for blocker module (`Ẩn mục này` / `Hiện mục này`) similar to updates panel for cleaner scrolling control. Evidence: `toggleBlockers(...)` function added and bound to `toggleBlockersBtn`; service restarted and HTML verification confirms control present. RAG: GREEN (UX request delivered). Owners: Huy AI (frontend toggle), Mạnh AI (deploy/restart), PM validation MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: none. Next: optional persist collapsed state in browser localStorage if user wants sticky preference.\n- 07:21 UTC: Heartbeat check request received with system status context. Decision: HEARTBEAT.md contains only template/comments and no actionable heartbeat tasks; ignore prior context per instruction. Owners: PM (MINH AI). ETA: immediate. Blockers: none. Next: return HEARTBEAT_OK.\n- 07:51 UTC: Heartbeat check request. Decision: HEARTBEAT.md unchanged (template/comments only), so no action required. Owners: PM (MINH AI). ETA: immediate. Blockers: none. Next: return HEARTBEAT_OK.\n- 08:00 UTC: Cron hourly report generated (VN, RAG) based on latest evidence logs/system status. Decision: giữ tổng thể GREEN cho 